# Flutter Widget Rules

## Widget Type

- Default to `StatelessWidget`
- Use `StatefulWidget` only for genuinely local mutable state (animations, form inputs)
- Always use `const` constructors where possible
- Always include `super.key` in the constructor

```dart
class MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  const MyWidget({super.key, required this.title});
  final String title;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) { ... }
}
```

## File Location

| Widget category | Path |
|---|---|
| Dashboard summary cards | `lib/widgets/dashboard/` |
| Habit-related | `lib/widgets/habits/` |
| Vision board | `lib/widgets/vision_board/` |
| Navigation | `lib/widgets/navigation/` |
| Dialogs | `lib/widgets/dialogs/` |
| Ads | `lib/widgets/ads/` |
| Canvas manipulation | `lib/widgets/manipulation/` |
| Routine/ritual | `lib/widgets/rituals/` |
| Insights | `lib/widgets/insights/` |
| General reusable | `lib/widgets/` |

## Standard Imports

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import '../../utils/app_colors.dart';
import '../../utils/app_spacing.dart';
import '../../utils/app_typography.dart';
```

## Card Pattern

```dart
final isDark = Theme.of(context).brightness == Brightness.dark;

Container(
  decoration: AppColors.cloudDecoration(isDark: isDark),
  padding: const EdgeInsets.all(AppSpacing.md),
  child: Column(
    crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,
    children: [
      Text('Title', style: AppTypography.heading3(context)),
      const SizedBox(height: AppSpacing.sm),
      Text('Body', style: AppTypography.body(context)),
    ],
  ),
)
```

## Colour Rules (non-negotiable)

- Page background → `AppColors.skyDecoration(isDark: isDark)`
- Card/content → `AppColors.cloudDecoration(isDark: isDark)`
- Primary button → `colorScheme.primary`
- Amber text → `AppColors.honeyText` (NEVER `AppColors.seedGold` for text)
- Mood/journal → `AppColors.lavenderDew`
- Chips/tags → `AppColors.sageContainer` background

See `morning-garden-colors` rule for full table.

## Spacing

Use `AppSpacing.*` constants — no hardcoded numbers.

## Typography

Use `AppTypography.*` or `Theme.of(context).textTheme.*` — no standalone `TextStyle` with `fontFamily`.

## Doc Comments

Add a one-line doc comment on every public widget class:

```dart
/// Displays the user's current habit streak with a progress ring.
class HabitStreakCard extends StatelessWidget { ... }
```
